::PC_U02_L05_Q01::
Question ID: PC_U02_L05_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.PC.EX.1
Question:
Which statement correctly interprets an exponential model?
{
=A. The coefficient is the initial value when x = 0.#Correct. In a model such as a(b^x), a is the starting output.
~B. A base between 0 and 1 shows growth.#This reverses decay; a base between 0 and 1 shows decay.
~C. A base greater than 1 shows decay.#This reverses growth; a base greater than 1 shows growth.
~D. The exponent is never connected to time.#The exponent often represents time or repeated intervals.
}
